  "body": "Adds the two STEP fixture verdict rows that the v0.19.0 release gate found missing from `step_files_agree_or_refuse_by_name` (`crates/kernel/tests/step_agreement.rs`). No fixture, golden or product code changed.\n\nRows added, with the verdicts measured in `gate-logs/release-20261113-113616/02-kernel_suites.log`:\n- `bad_entity_mid_data.step`: import \"both refuse (solidcore: read_step: invalid input: STEP syntax error)\", mesh \"no exact solid to judge against\". A refusal by name on both sides, so it is kept as a refusal rather than an agreement.\n- `lathe_holder_offset.step`: import \"agree\", mesh \"watertight, within tolerance\".\n\nBoth fixtures are in millimetres (`SI_UNIT(.MILLI.,.METRE.)`), so `mm_per_unit: 1.0`, the same default the test already used for them. The existing rows' verdicts are unchanged.\n\nPinned by: `step_files_agree_or_refuse_by_name` (`cargo test --release -p camcraft-kernel --test step_agreement`: 1 passed).\n\nNot exercised: the rest of the release tier. Only this suite was run.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #1400\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
